# Track every request in loop-tasks.md

When the user makes a **new feature, fix, content, or process request**, log it in `loop-tasks.md` before or as you start work. Do not skip logging even if you implement immediately.

## On new request

1. Add a row under the right section (prefer **§0** Priority when it is active work; otherwise the matching numbered section).
2. Status: `[todo]` if queued, `[doing]` if you start now.
3. Prefer extending a weaker/existing row over creating a duplicate identical row.

## While working

- Keep the row at `[doing]`.
- Update wording if scope clarifies mid-task.

## On completion

- Mark `[done]` with a brief conclusion (one short line).
- Do **not** claim suite/smoke proof while testing is disabled (see `no-testing.mdc`).
- Use `[blocked]` when stuck on a real dependency; say what blocks it.

## Examples

```markdown
- [doing] Click-walk pauses auto-attack until path ends.
- [done] Campfire heal within 5 tiles + effect radius ring. — Conclusion: regen radius 5; ring GFX matches combat range style.
```
